0..67 Comment "// A presented type whose constructor holds a continuation. A field"
68..134 Comment "// written `A => T` is the description code\'s function former, the"
135..212 Comment "// higher-order descriptions\' `Π` over a type of arguments (Chapman, Dagand,"
213..278 Comment "// McBride and Morris, _The Gentle Art of Levitation_, ICFP 2010,"
279..354 Comment "// doi:10.1145/1863543.1863547). It decodes to the thunked arrow the native"
355..434 Comment "// reading gives the same field, so the type keeps its rule. Programs that read"
435..511 Comment "// and store a state are state\'s free model, and put-put is the law of state"
512..582 Comment "// a store obeys (Plotkin and Power, _Notions of computation determine"
583..631 Comment "// monads_, 2002, doi:10.1007/3-540-45931-6_24)."
632..634 Comment "//"
635..650 Comment "// - see: #2511"
652..717 Comment "/// Programs over an integer state: a read hands the state to its"
718..786 Comment "/// continuation, and a store the next store overwrites is no store."
